// The tether (bible 8.1 Lantern Chain; character-bibles.md §2, Act 2). At the Lantern Chain's tether-post, Sable sells
// the cord to the faded third lighthouse, then rows it herself. It opens Aury's Lighthouse (`saltmarrow.tether`).
// Voice: clipped; names the price of everything; ends conversations first; never "I hope".

title: Chain_Sable_Tether
---
<<if not has_flag("act2.started") or not has_flag("saltmarrow.sable.aury")>>
    Sable: Tether-post. Cords to places that aren't there. Not for sale to you. Yet. #still #face:wary #line:08d877c
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("sable.tether_sold")>>
    Sable: Cord's tied. Boat's here. Go, or I'm rowing without you. #still #line:0415600
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Sable: Third lighthouse. You asked who keeps it. Now you're going. #line:05417ab
Sable: Tether's fifteen. My rowing's free. Don't read anything into that. #face:wary #line:009336b
-> Fifteen. Done. #line:035710a
    Sable: Fair price. Only fair one on this coast. #line:0064794
    <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
-> Why is the rowing free? #line:0c8dc7f
    Sable: Because I'm not selling him. Get in. #face:grave #line:02c533e
    <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
-> ... #line:02d3f93
    Sable: Good. He talks enough for both of you. #face:bright #line:0cff421
    <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
Sable: Remember. He doesn't know. Don't tell him. That's a favour, not a price. #face:grave #line:0e60b3f
Sable: And this. Ferryman's charter. Comes with the cord. Price is you come back. #face:bright #line:07e5a7d
<<charter Ferryman>>
<<flag sable.tether_sold 1>>
<<flag saltmarrow.tether 1>>
===
